A computer is an electronic machine that takes raw data as input, processes it using stored instructions, and produces meaningful information as output.
Main Components
• Hardware: The physical parts of a computer, including the Central Processing Unit (CPU), memory (RAM), storage drives (SSD/HDD), and input/output devices.
• Software: The programs and operating systems that give step-by-step instructions to the hardware on how to function.
• CPU (Central Processing Unit): The core brain of the system that performs logical and arithmetic calculations.
